<h2 class="design">Ian's Peace</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">'i wanted to see what he loved'</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.newsobserver.com/lifestyles/extras/story/766682.html">Watch this (thanks, MEM)</a>: On June 23, News &amp; Observer photojournalists Travis Long, Takaaki Iwabu, Ethan Hyman, and Juli Leonard visited the Eno Quarry in Durham to shoot video and still images for an in-house project on the quarry. The group had envisioned a light piece on swimming hole culture.<br />
<br />
A few weeks later, they were contacted by the family of 19-year-old Ian Creath, who had drowned in the quarry on July 9. The family sought the last-known video and photographs of him.
